sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: captured Instance Schedule definitions, flow-tighten rule 14. Native child completion is the installation receipt.
  %% status: migrated
  %% kind: schedule.install_instance_definitions
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>Instance runtime
  Note over GW: Capture definitions<br/>Instance 42
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - capture the existing definition copies and their public runtime intent
  %%> - keep the admitted owner and Node for every member
  GW->>SW: Start one run<br/>captured members
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - each Schedule UUID, desired state and SSH host pins
  %%> - no Schedule command or execution credential is copied into the parent
  loop each captured copy
    SW->>N: members
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the existing child installs the captured service and timer with official cfgmgmt resources
    %%> - copies share one Node and converge in sequence; a disabled copy stays stopped
  end
  Note over SW: Check the members
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - native assert confirms that all expanded member steps succeeded
  %%> - an empty captured set completes without Node work
  alt native run succeeded
    SW-->>GW: Native completion<br/>all members installed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the existing history read confirms the end check; no shell prints a completion marker
    Note over GW: Record installed copies<br/>keep desired state
    %%> Result:
    %%> - mark the captured copies active without enabling a disabled timer
  else a member failed
    N--xSW: Native member failure
    %%> Result:
    %%> - keep completed Node changes and the captured definition records
    SW--xGW: Native failed result<br/>failed step and error code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - mark the captured copies failed so the owner can investigate and rerun
  end
